WEBVTT

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.330
"This is a work of fiction. The characters,
organizations, and names herein are fictitious,
and bear no relation to existing entities."

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:41.250
"Ikebukuro West Gate Park"

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:03.790
"Majima Produce"

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:08.040
"3-Year-Old Falls from Balcony"

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:11.080
Hello.

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:15.750
Kyouichi, and Isogai.

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.790
What brings you out here?

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:22.330
I have a request for Ikebukuro's
capable troubleshooter.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:23.370
Huh?

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:44.620
Several days ago, a small child
had a fall at a Senkawa apartment.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:45.080
Yeah.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:45.870
"3-Year-Old Falls from Balcony"

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:45.870
Yeah.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:47.250
"3-Year-Old Falls from Balcony"

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:47.250
You mean this.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:50.330
He's three, with a single mother.

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:52.200
Could you go check in on them?

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.040
Huh?!

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:56.370
The two of them often come by our park.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:12.620
The mother watches Kyouichi dance
while she lets her boy play.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:19.580
But several days ago, she came
by herself. Without her child.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:21.950
"He apparently fell while
playing on the balcony,

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:24.870
while his mother was out by herself."

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:25.870
Was that when?

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:26.950
Yes.

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:28.120
And these are posts in response to that article.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:30.370
"This is why I can't stand single mothers."
"She's irresponsible."
"That's the problem with single mothers."
And these are posts in response to that article.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:31.870
"Don't have children if you can't raise them."

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:33.120
"Unfit mother"

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.700
I'd like to take the ones who made those posts,

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:42.790
line them up, and mow them
down with a machine gun.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.830
Yui Ohnuki, age 22. Kazushi, age 3.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:53.120
Kyouichi and I have only spoken
with them once or twice.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:58.200
If you've hardly ever talked to them,
why are you being so supportive?

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:04.580
Because she's a fan of my dancing.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:06.830
You have to take care of your fans.

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:08.160
Right...

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:09.540
Makoto!

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:10.620
What?!

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:13.000
You go and check on them.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:13.950
Huh?!

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:17.620
I can't just ignore it
when I hear "single mother."

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:19.910
Hello there, ma'am.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:20.830
This is our--

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:24.500
Kyouichi-kun. I've heard about you from Makoto.

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:28.580
Heck, you're a lot more
handsome than what I imagined.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.620
What were you imagining?

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:33.750
Never you mind!

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.500
Now, hurry and go!

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:39.290
Hold on a minute! There's no
reason for <i>you </i>to be so eager!

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:40.370
I'm the one who got the reque--

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:43.410
Then as of now, I'm seconding the request.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.790
Go and take these to them.

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:49.040
The small ones taste best this time of year.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:50.620
Go and share them.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.250
"Troubleshooter"?

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:58.700
Bananas! Bananas! Bananas! Bananas!

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:00.950
We have company, quiet down!

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:02.370
Ugh...

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:05.040
Our Kyouichi was concerned.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:11.330
He asked Makoto-san here to help out,
in case you two were having trouble.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:15.660
But why is he concerned about us?

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:18.500
That's the kind of guy Kyouichi is.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:23.500
It's a good thing Kazushi-kun's
injuries were no big deal.

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:30.410
I've been striving so hard since he was born.

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:33.950
That's why I thought I could get away with it.

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:35.870
"Get away with it"?

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:39.250
My man ran off while I was pregnant.

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:42.620
That's why I can't collect child support.

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:46.870
I've been working like crazy since he was born.

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:49.160
Where do you work now?

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:52.410
A plant in Ouji where they make
convenience store box lunches.

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:58.080
I'm on my feet working from
10 PM to 5 AM, and when I get home,

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:02.620
I make breakfast for Kazushi,
and then nap during the day.

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:06.080
I play with him some,
then snatch whatever sleep I can.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:08.790
You don't have much in the way of time.

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:11.950
It's not just time. I don't have money, either.

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:16.660
For working all night, five nights a week,
I get a little over ¥160,000.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:19.120
That's how it is for contract employees.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:22.200
Things like taxes and insurance
get deducted from that,

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:29.080
and the rent here is 70,000, so I'm not
sure how I can cut costs any further.

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:33.040
I've gotten lots of calls from
newspapers and magazines, too.

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:36.290
I'm so fed up with it.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.660
That banana was good, wasn't it?

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:42.040
Yeah! Banana!

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:43.950
Can I just call you "Kazushi"?

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:45.080
Sure!

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:47.080
Why don't we all go to a family restaurant!

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.000
Huh?

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.250
Family restaurant! Family restaurant!

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:52.700
Oh, it's not out of pity.

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:55.450
My mom's a single mother, too,

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:59.080
so I know how much of a pain that stuff can be.

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:01.120
And I'm hungry.

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:11.370
Can I ask you something?

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:13.830
You were always with Kazushi,

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:18.200
but that day, you went alone
to watch Kyouichi dance. How come?

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:27.120
I was always on a walk with Kazushi,
so I would only catch glimpses.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:33.620
But I thought his dancing looked so good,
and I wanted to take my time watching.

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:37.290
That day, I wanted to watch by myself so badly.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:38.910
Gotcha.

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:44.500
It's so hard.

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:49.330
I'm standing on the edge of a cliff.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:54.120
That's the story.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:56.290
So, what do we do now?

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:58.580
Keep an eye on them a bit longer.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:05.080
Fine, but just watching isn't going
to change anything about their situation.

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.950
Your mother...

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:09.200
Huh?

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:14.410
Never mind, tell her this:
"The small ones were superb."

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:21.450
She's already falling?

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:28.160
Yeah. Yui-chan's not on the edge of a cliff,
she's already starting to fall off.

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:31.160
If something isn't done, she'll be in trouble.

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:34.790
Ritsuko-san.

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:42.290
Hello.

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:44.410
What's going on?

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:46.080
A little something good.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:48.910
Hey, Kazushi.

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:51.040
Kazushi, what do we say?

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.620
Hello...

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:57.080
Hello.

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:58.660
See you later.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:05.040
What the heck is--

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:06.660
She's got a man.

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:07.540
Huh?

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:09.910
You think so, too, ma'am?

00:09:09.910 --> 00:09:12.660
--Huh?
--Oh, Yoshioka-san.

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:14.950
Has Yui done something wrong?

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:16.410
I can't go into detail,

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:22.080
but a nasty sex industry scout's
been showing up around here lately.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:25.700
It starts with him flirting with
a woman, and dating like normal,

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:28.370
but then he buys her more and more luxury goods,

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:31.120
then when the time seems right,
he picks a fight with her.

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:36.250
"Pay me back for all the gifts
and food I've bought you."

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:38.790
If she refuses, then it's
off to the sex industry.

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:41.580
Luxury goods as gifts...

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:44.910
"A little something good," she said.

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:49.250
His group makes a killing by collecting
referral fees from sex joints.

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:51.500
We've been keeping an eye
on women likely to be targeted,

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:54.160
hoping to catch the guys in the act.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.700
But they're good at not getting caught.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:59.250
You were watching Yui?

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:05.250
They go after single mothers
who have trouble making ends meet.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.580
If anything happens, let me know.

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:11.620
Okay, I'm going to go keep
an eye on another lady.

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:14.700
He just told me to follow Yui around.

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:17.120
Don't take your eyes off her.

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:19.290
They're not dropping <i>her </i>into the sex industry!

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:20.870
Okay, fine.

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:24.450
But, hey, isn't the sex
industry still a business?

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:27.540
I mean, it's nothing to be proud of,
but it's not shameful either.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:31.620
You're an idiot! Men and women
look at these things differently!

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:33.160
Now get going!

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:41.000
"Episode 8"

00:10:52.870 --> 00:10:54.620
"Realistic action!"

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:29.700
"Rose Castle Café"

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:42.910
Yeah, that's right. She just left.

00:11:42.910 --> 00:11:45.750
She just needs one more push.

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:48.660
Okay, good luck to you, too.

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:50.790
What's your problem?!

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:52.620
S-Sorry!

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:53.910
Huh?!

00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:55.950
Like I said, what's your problem?!

00:11:55.950 --> 00:12:00.120
Hey, buddy, aren't those a really
nice pair of Rocco Sandiegos?!

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:01.910
Wh-What about them?

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:04.870
Collecting shoes is a hobby of mine.

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:07.910
But I don't have much loot,
so not many shoes, either.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:10.950
Loot? You're in <i>that </i>line of work, huh?

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:14.580
Well, it's not all that big a thing.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:17.330
I get to be an errand boy for the Hidaka Group.

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:18.620
The Hidaka Group?

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:23.700
Yeah. Their PR Department head and I
were buddies in middle school.

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:24.700
Oh?

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:27.750
The PR head of the Hidaka Group...

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:30.910
Tell me a little more about that.

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:37.080
You, too, huh?

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:39.290
That's right.

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:45.250
So, who do I gotta talk to to deal with
the sex joints the Hidaka Group runs?

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:48.870
Huh? Sex joints?

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:53.160
The truth is, I'm an expert sex industry scout.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:56.290
Really, you are?! Wild!

00:12:56.290 --> 00:13:01.330
Yeah. But then, I only just started
working here in Ikebukuro.

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:02.750
Wow!

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:07.290
Okay then, how do you drop
a hot lady into the sex industry?

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:09.290
You don't drop her in.

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:12.080
She's the one who falls in.

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:16.200
Just find a woman who's
in trouble or suffering.

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:19.830
Single mothers are perfect for it.

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:24.160
Is there one you're going after now, then?

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:26.450
Lean in a little.

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:30.080
You remember that recent
falling incident in Senkawa?

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.450
I've snared the mother from that.

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:37.330
Hell, it's not like I even do much.

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:41.500
I caught a broad who
fell off a cliff, that's all.

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:46.450
She's the type who can't get by
unless someone looks after her.

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:51.080
Thank you very much!

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:52.580
See ya!

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:00.830
Screw that shit!

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:05.080
Yui's... struggling just to survive!

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:08.750
"Rose Castle Café"

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:13.040
You talk a big game, kid,
but you're surprisingly capable.

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:17.290
Just a day later, and here you're already
introducing me to the PR head.

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:19.370
Thanks.

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:21.200
Oh, here we go.

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:31.950
Yui?

00:14:31.950 --> 00:14:33.540
Why're <i>you </i>here?

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:35.540
And who's this older lady?

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:38.450
You must be the disgusting bum.

00:14:38.450 --> 00:14:40.620
Hey, what the...?

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:42.330
Who the hell are you guys?!

00:14:42.330 --> 00:14:44.120
We're fruit vendors!

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:45.250
Huh?!

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:46.950
Let him hear it.

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:50.410
You don't drop her in.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:53.080
She's the one who falls in.

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:57.290
Just find a woman who's
in trouble or suffering.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:00.540
Single mothers are perfect for it.

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:03.330
What's the big idea?!

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:11.330
Ikebukuro Police, Community Safety Division.

00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:13.200
Shinji Naganuma, you're under arrest

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:17.160
for suspicion of violating the
Prostitution Prevention Law, Article 9,

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:21.160
and the Employment Security Act,
Article 63, paragraph 2.

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:23.580
Come with us to the station.

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:26.120
Suspect apprehended at 1:25 PM.

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:28.160
--Naganuma, hand over the cell.
--Don't touch me!

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:30.120
You goddamn pigs!

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:31.540
Hand it over!

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:43.200
Your mother is quite a gem.
Take good care of her.

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:45.790
Yui-chan, come with me.

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:47.500
We need to talk.

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:56.500
Kazushi, hold still a second.

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:06.830
It was several days ago when I noticed.

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:10.000
Kazushi was suddenly depressed.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:13.910
Raising one's hand against a child
due to stress is common enough.

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:17.750
But haven't Kazushi's antics
been irritating you more often

00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:20.870
since you got to know that guy?

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:33.450
Since that accident happened,
I've been at a loss for what to do.

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:40.620
But even when I give everything I have,
they tell me that's just how things work.

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:44.410
I stay up all night working,
and raise a child during the day.

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:48.790
I try to have a bit of fun,
and they tell me I'm an unfit mother.

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:52.200
After the accident, they said I should die...

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:02.160
Sometimes, I get so aggravated with my child.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:06.250
If it weren't for him,
I could look for full-time work,

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:10.330
and dress up nicely, and even
fall in love with someone.

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:13.250
That it's all because of him...

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:16.250
Because of the child of a man I don't even love.

00:17:25.950 --> 00:17:27.580
Mommy, don't cry.

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:29.500
Not your fault!

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:44.620
Does it hurt no matter what?

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:48.750
It does! What that guy said is true!

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:51.540
I'm standing on the edge of a cliff.

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:54.500
Maybe I'm already falling.

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:57.620
Okay, okay. Then you should...

00:17:57.620 --> 00:17:59.410
...give up your child.

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:04.330
You can't go on living like this.

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:06.830
You might end up killing your child.

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:09.410
So, give him up.

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:13.540
Like I once did.

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:16.000
You... serious?!

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:19.580
You tried so hard it wrecked you,
and it still wasn't enough.

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:23.000
Nobody would blame you for giving up your child.

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:24.830
Besides, I say "give him up," but I just mean

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:28.120
have someone look after him long enough
for you to get your life in order.

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:30.250
It's nothing to be ashamed of.

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:34.660
I went and talked to a caseworker
I've known for some time.

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:39.830
Makoto's father died in an
accident soon after he was born.

00:18:39.830 --> 00:18:43.000
All I had left was the store
and a huge pile of debt.

00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:45.540
All I could do was work alone.

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:49.450
I decided to place baby Makoto
in someone else's custody.

00:18:52.870 --> 00:18:58.120
For a whole two years right after he was born,
I never even so much as nursed him.

00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:03.790
Again and again, I thought I was a bad mother.
That I'd abandoned my child.

00:19:03.790 --> 00:19:08.830
But I refused to stop working like hell.
I paid off the debt and saved up.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:11.870
When things were ready, I went and got him.

00:19:11.870 --> 00:19:15.410
As you can see, he managed to grow up.

00:19:15.410 --> 00:19:19.450
We don't have a lot of money,
but if someone in this town's in trouble,

00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:22.950
he'll run around trying to help,
regardless of what happens to himself.

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:25.910
He's turned out to be quite a man.

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:34.660
Listen, Yui-chan. Your boy's sure to grow up,
and he'll say some mean things.

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:37.620
Like "Drop dead, you old hag."

00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:42.910
It's okay, Mommy. Not your fault!

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:57.540
That's the first time I've heard that story.

00:19:57.540 --> 00:20:01.200
I'm no gem. Not at all.

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:03.000
Yeah, I'll say.

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:05.160
That's right.

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:06.660
Yui-chan.

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:12.540
Kyouichi says, "You can do it."

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:18.160
He wants to dance for you and Kazu-kun.

00:20:44.790 --> 00:20:49.700
When Kyouichi was little and living
in Chicago, he lost his parents.

00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:51.790
He said it was a traffic accident.

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:59.410
After that, he grew up by himself in Chicago.

00:20:59.410 --> 00:21:01.950
All while working hard to learn ballet.

00:21:01.950 --> 00:21:07.290
I think that must be why
he's preoccupied with "family."

00:21:07.290 --> 00:21:11.580
No matter what form a family may take.

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:16.450
Maybe Kyouichi's envious.

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:18.410
The airplane guy.

00:21:18.410 --> 00:21:20.830
Yeah, that's right.

00:21:20.830 --> 00:21:22.700
Airplanes fly through the sky, don't they?

00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:23.790
Yep.

00:21:23.790 --> 00:21:28.830
From now on, you and your mom
can fly all you want, too.

00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:30.620
Into the huge sky.

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:31.660
Really?

00:21:31.660 --> 00:21:33.790
Yeah, really.

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:53.790
Yui temporarily put Kazushi in a home
and started searching for regular employment.

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:56.950
She had been suffering,
not even aware there were terms

00:21:56.950 --> 00:22:00.290
like "childcare allowance" or "caseworker."

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:05.290
But this town wouldn't
forsake a mother like her.

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:10.540
It wouldn't trot out the buzzword
"self-responsibility," and cast her aside.

00:22:10.540 --> 00:22:14.000
That's the kind of town I think this is.
